# MCU Timeout Recovery - Patches Working
# Date: 2026-01-13 00:30
# Kernel: 6.18.4-3-cachyos-wifi-fix (with 17 MT7925 patches)
# Status: RECOVERED - No crash, patches prevented kernel panic

## Summary
Multiple MCU command timeouts occurred during reassociation. The patched kernel
recovered gracefully by reloading firmware and reconnecting. NO KERNEL PANIC.
This demonstrates the patches are working as intended.

## Trigger
AP temporarily rejected reassociation (status 30 = comeback later), followed by
association timeout, which triggered a cascade of MCU timeouts.

## Key Observation
- 5 consecutive MCU timeouts
- Firmware auto-reloaded
- Brief reconnection dance with fallback AP
- Successfully reconnected to MLD AP with both links
- **NO CRASH** - on unpatched kernel this would have caused NULL pointer panic

## Bluetooth Impact
The MT7925 combo chip's Bluetooth side also experienced errors during recovery:
  Opcode 0x2041 failed: -16 (start background scanning failed)
This suggests the MCU timeout affects both WiFi and BT subsystems.

## Timeline
1. AP rejected reassociation temporarily (comeback 898 TU)
2. Association timed out
3. MCU timeouts began (5 in succession)
4. Firmware reloaded
5. Brief auth/deauth dance with fallback AP
6. Successfully reconnected to main MLD AP
7. Both links established (2.4GHz + 5GHz)

## Final State After Recovery
Connected to d8:b3:70:f8:9e:7b (MLD AP)
  Link 0: d8:b3:70:f8:9e:7c @ 2437 MHz
  Link 1: d8:b3:70:f8:9e:7d @ 5765 MHz
  Signal: -39 dBm
  TX: 1200.9 Mbit/s EHT-MCS 11
  Ping: 0% packet loss

